{"Title":"An Act relative to means tested senior citizen property tax exemptions in the town of Westford","BillNumber":"H4920","DocketNumber":"HD5270","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J_A1","Name":"James Arciero","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_A1","ResponseDate":"2024-07-17T15:37:32.653"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"J_A1","Name":"James Arciero","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_A1","ResponseDate":"2024-07-17T15:37:32.6533333"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"JJC0","Name":"John J. Cronin","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JJC0","ResponseDate":"2024-07-17T15:37:32.653"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4920/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Arciero of Westford and Senator Cronin, a joint petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 4920) of James Arciero (by vote of the town) relative to means tested senior citizen property tax exemptions in the town of Westford.  Revenue.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1     Section 2 of chapter 324 of the acts of 2020 is hereby amended by striking out the words: \"that in no event shall property taxes be reduced by more than 50 per cent by this exemption\" and inserting in place thereof the following words:- that in no event shall the amount of the exemption constitute more than 50 per cent of the property tax.\r\n\tSECTION 2     Section 3 of said chapter 314 is hereby amended by striking out clause (e) and inserting in place thereof the following clause:-\r\n\t       (e) the maximum assessed value of the domicile does not exceed the prior year's average assessed value of a single family for the town;.\r\n\tSECTION 3     Section 4 of said chapter 314 is hereby amended by striking out the word \"selectmen\" and inserting in place thereof the following words:- select board.\r\n\tSECTION 4     Said chapter 314 is hereby further amended by striking out sections 9 and 10. \r\n\tSECTION 5     This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}